[gd_scene load_steps=5 format=3]

; Package 11 A8 — rewritten to the HUD_CONTRACT (F24) hierarchy.
;
; SafeArea / TopLeft_Panel / TopRight_Panel replace the old
; Root / {TopLeft, Portrait, Vitals} split, and the widgets StoryHUD.cs used to
; build at runtime "so the authored scene stays untouched" (the Rally echo band,
; the Integrity readout, the boss intro card) are authored nodes now. The fourth,
; the V7.3 manual-rewind cooldown pip, is deleted rather than moved: F03 retires
; the 12 s manual rewind it measured.
;
; The repo extras the contract does not enumerate — LevelTitle/Objective,
; BossPanel, CheckpointToast — are kept as named siblings under SafeArea and
; recorded as accepted deviations. They are shipped behaviour, not drift.
;
; Only genuinely DATA-DRIVEN counts are still built in code: the block-charge
; pips (base capacity plus the Story-only Resonance bonus) and the Act III anchor
; pips. Authoring a fixed number there would cap the HUD at today's defaults.
;
; Package 12 W10 (M15): BeaconAnchors sits immediately right of the rewind
; hourglass (RewindCounter), ahead of the TimeFreezeIndicator, per HUD_CONTRACT;
; the indicator stays its own node, never attached to the rewind counter.

